content.p:
 After realisation, the third party may assert the claims to which it is entitled under civil law in the event of theft, loss or other misappropriation of a movable item (Arts 934 and 935 CC

 SR 210
	) or in the event of bad faith on the part of the acquirer (Arts 936 and 974 para. 3 CC) outside the debt enforcement proceedings. A public auction within the meaning of Article 934 paragraph 2 CC shall also be deemed to be a private sale in accordance with Article 130 of this Act.

